{"id":"795aa5cd-c2a3-49e2-bcbd-925d5a670a71","expr":"(byte1 & 0xFF) >= 0xC2","rationale":"As byte values are signed in Java, casting to int and masking is a way to compare unsigned bytes. The method checks if byte1 is at least 0xC2 in unsigned terms.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"org.apache.dubbo.common.utils.DecodeUtil#checkUtf8(byte,byte):void","file":"org/apache/dubbo/common/utils/Utf8Utils.java","createdAt":"2026-09-10T20:13:47.326873715Z"}
